  "protocol_amendment_recommendation": "Protocol Amendment Recommendation ADR-005 Section 11: 1. Separation of Evidence: Physical evaluation evidence is rooted in 528 physical speakers (Cohort 1 with 60 speakers and Cohort 2 with 468 speakers, evaluated on Tesla T4 GPU). The CV27 benchmark dataset is a calibrated simulation fixture (N=96 rows, namespace synth_cv27_*) modeling a hypothesized Delta_D = -2.00 pp selective adaptation effect. 2. Cross-Cohort Integrity: The 900 clips in Cohort 1 and 7,020 clips in Cohort 2 are mutually disjoint with zero recording ID overlap, zero speaker ID overlap, 100% unique summary rows, and 100% recomputed Levenshtein edit distance agreement. 3. Confirmatory Sample Size: Under the scenario Delta_D = -2.00 pp effect size, the preliminary draft design of N=78 speakers per stratum provides only approximately 40.7% joint power [32.7%, 49.0%] and is strictly UNDERPOWERED. At N=210, estimated power reaches 89.33% [83.3%, 93.8%] (near target). At N=220, estimated power reaches 95.00% with a 95% Clopper-Pearson LCB of 91.00% >= 90.0% in the fresh independent simulation with non-overlapping trajectories (seed=20261028), strictly satisfying Decision Rule B (LCB >= 90%) conditional on the calibrated scenario simulation assumptions. Both exploratory and independent confirmatory evaluations recommend adopting N=220 speakers per stratum (1,320 total confirmatory speakers, 19,800 clips) in the formal protocol amendment. Confirmatory Cohort 3 unsealing remains on HOLD pending formal protocol amendment, physical audio manifest locking, and independent governance authorization."
